"A1 iteration 5 is finished. The engine is now `e3-1.7.0` and the change record is at `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/docs/production/runlog/a1/iter_5/CHANGE.md`. BROAD recall cannot reach 0.80 without fitting label errors: 36 of its 39 misses are label problems, not engine misses.\n\n**Starting point.** This was the second start of iteration 5. The first start had taken the snapshot `engine_before.tgz` (sha `bee17fa9\u2026`), which equals iteration 4's final engine. It then made fixes A and B and ran the tests, the physical set and the G1 tier, but stopped before writing a record. I kept that snapshot and confirmed the engine still matched those runs. The previous generality check was clean, so nothing was removed. Iteration 4's one regression (50757000_02_X) was fixed rather than reverted.\n\n**BROAD recall audit (owner direction)**\n- I compared each BROAD miss with the gold of record on the same scan: the Gold11 relabel on the 9 Gold11 scans, GOLD_SET_V1 elsewhere.\n- 36 of the 39 misses are label problems:\n  - 20 human Gold11 lines sit 4.2-14.7 mm off the apex, beyond the matcher's 4 mm gate.\n  - 6 human lines are merged across separate folds.\n  - 6 human lines lie where there is no fold.\n  - 4 come from the old 11979003 labels, which split a window-interrupted fold into two lines.\n- Only 3 are engine misses:\n  - two hooks bent the wrong way on 23553000 SCAN_2;\n  - one fold on 28870000 FULL that the recipe excludes.\n- The best reachable recall on the frozen BROAD gold is therefore 0.75.\n- On the same 24 scans against the gold of record, the engine scores precision 0.987, recall 0.981 and family-macro F1 0.972. The best F1 lane scores precision 0.679, recall 0.475 and family-macro F1 0.581.\n- Of the 54 BROAD false positives, 52 match a gold-of-record line. The other 2 are a stage-level convention case on 38172000 SCAN_1: the gold merges two collinear folds into one line.\n\n**Engine changes (general rules only; frozen thresholds and `eval/`/`compile/` untouched)**\n- **Fixes A and B (first start).**\n  - A: a line seen on one sheet surface is also read as the other surface when that surface is seen just outside the search window.\n  - B: a formed reading more than 8\u00b0 off nominal now also triggers the wide search.\n  - Together they repair the iteration-4 regression on 50757000_02_X; only that scan changes.\n  - The new ~4.8 mm position FAILs on that scan look like a real off-nominal part: its sister scan reads within 0.4 mm.\n- **Fix C (this start).** The bend angle is now signed by which side of the parent the flange lies on.\n  - Before, a bend formed the wrong way read its angle magnitude as if formed correctly. A shallow bend (about 11\u00b0 or less) fully reversed would have PASSed.\n  - Now such a bend reads above 180\u00b0 and always FAILs. Its lengths and position are reported UNKNOWN.\n  - The angle magnitude is unchanged, so every correctly formed bend reads exactly as before. Results are identical on all 26 runnable physical cases, the G1 tier and all 113 CAD-stage probes.\n  - Synthetic wrong-way probes confirm the new FAIL behaviour.\n\n**Results**\n\n| Measure | Iteration 4 | Now | Best F1 lane |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GOLD_SET_V1 micro / family-macro | 0.977 / 0.966 | 0.990 / 0.974 | 0.566 / 0.583 |\n| Gold11 relabel F1 | 0.987 | 0.987 | 0.547 |\n| BROAD (frozen) family-macro / recall | 0.806 / 0.708 | 0.814 / 0.729 | 0.543 / 0.451 |\n| Per-bend correctness given CAD | 0.872 | 0.892 | \u2013 |\n\n- 20 of the 22 bends not counted correct are limited by things outside the engine:\n  - a flange ending at a bend not yet formed in a staged scan (8);\n  - a missing compile nominal (4);\n  - disputed truth rows (5);\n  - the line convention (2);\n  - a rolled part (1).\n- The other 2 are the wrong-way hooks.\n- The false-PASS proxy is unchanged at 3, all explained.\n- **Tests:** 142 passed (11 new).\n- **G1:** PASS, every accuracy value identical to iteration 4.\n- **CAD-stage probes:** 113 probes; 0 wrong states, 0 invalid, 0 angle false PASS or false FAIL (iteration 4's sweep had 4 wrong states).\n- **Still failing:**\n  - G2(a), because the gate of record is still the human Gold11: F1 0.391 against the best lane's 0.473.\n  - G2(f), because the 15651004 \"repeats\" are three different stages.\n  - G3, because of the disputed 10839000 scan_2 truth rows, the rolled 28870000 SCAN_1, and a known-good angle error of 1.186\u00b0 against a 1.0\u00b0 limit.\n  - None of these is limited by the engine on this data.\n\n**Next:** read wrong-way bends outside the current search range with a mirrored hinge search (the 2 hooks). Also try a wrong-part test limited to the recipe's supported panels for the rolled part.\n\nAll heavy jobs ran one at a time under the shared lock with `OMP_NUM_THREADS=1`. Nothing sealed or FRESH was opened.\n\nFiles are in `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/docs/production/runlog/a1/iter_5/`:\n- CHANGE.md\n- engine_before.tgz\n- engine.diff\n- validation/\n- diag/\n- tools/\n\nNew tests: `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/tests/test_prod_engine_inspect_a1_iter5.py`"